WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:02.974
Welcome to SysNDD.

00:03.107 --> 00:06.266
Let's find entities by their phenotypes.

00:06.633 --> 00:12.206
Which neurodevelopmental disorders
match a set of clinical features?

00:12.339 --> 00:18.345
Let's choose phenotypes, combine them,
read the result, and check a match.

00:18.700 --> 00:22.238
In the menu, open Tables, then Phenotypes.

00:22.371 --> 00:25.136
The page is called Phenotype search.

00:25.270 --> 00:29.024
Intellectual disability is already selected.

00:29.367 --> 00:33.049
Select the arrow at the right of the phenotype box.

00:33.182 --> 00:36.930
In Search phenotypes, type seizures, and select it.

00:37.064 --> 00:40.478
Add microcephaly the same way.

00:40.833 --> 00:47.207
SysNDD uses a fixed set of broad
terms from the Human Phenotype Ontology,

00:47.340 --> 00:51.298
or HPO, so that entities can be compared.

00:51.431 --> 00:54.196
Curators include a term when the feature occurs

00:54.329 --> 00:58.622
in 20 percent or more of affected individuals.

00:58.755 --> 01:03.677
The search reads these annotations,
not the clinical synopsis.

01:04.033 --> 01:06.777
Beside the box, AND is active.

01:06.911 --> 01:11.605
With AND, an entity must carry every selected phenotype.

01:11.739 --> 01:15.012
Each term you add makes the list shorter.

01:15.145 --> 01:19.384
Above the table,
the number of matching entities is shown.

01:19.733 --> 01:25.698
Select OR. Now one of the selected
phenotypes is enough, and the list grows.

01:25.831 --> 01:30.059
Select AND again to return to the shorter list.

01:30.400 --> 01:36.043
Use AND to narrow a differential
diagnosis to entities with all the features.

01:36.176 --> 01:40.881
Use OR to collect every entity with any of them.

01:41.233 --> 01:46.779
Each row is one entity: a gene,
a mode of inheritance and a disease.

01:46.913 --> 01:53.222
Here is <i>ARID1B</i> with Coffin-Siris syndrome 1,
autosomal dominant.

01:53.356 --> 01:58.329
In the evidence category column,
the green check means Definitive.

01:58.700 --> 02:01.483
Results can mix evidence categories.

02:01.616 --> 02:04.668
Here, the category filter is set to Definitive,

02:04.801 --> 02:07.399
so only Definitive entities remain.

02:07.532 --> 02:12.096
The .xlsx button downloads the whole list.

02:12.467 --> 02:14.034
Why check a match?

02:14.168 --> 02:17.620
A match only means the terms are recorded for an entity,

02:17.754 --> 02:19.750
not how often they occur.

02:19.883 --> 02:23.824
In Filter Symbol, type <i>SCN8A</i>.

02:23.958 --> 02:27.752
It appears in the result for all three phenotypes.

02:28.100 --> 02:30.842
Select the entity ID to open it.

02:30.976 --> 02:34.149
Under Phenotypes, each term has a modifier:

02:34.282 --> 02:37.664
present, uncertain, variable or rare.

02:37.798 --> 02:42.712
Phenotypes in green are
reported in at least 20% of cases.

02:42.845 --> 02:48.346
Phenotypes reported in fewer,
such as microcephaly, are uncertain.

02:48.700 --> 02:51.956
The search matches a term with any modifier.

02:52.090 --> 02:56.080
A match is an entity to check, not a diagnosis.

02:56.214 --> 02:58.883
Annotations may not list every feature,

02:59.016 --> 03:02.944
so a missing term is no proof of absence.

03:03.300 --> 03:06.742
Remember: AND narrows, OR widens.

03:06.875 --> 03:09.801
Filter the category before you use the list.

03:09.934 --> 03:14.569
And open the entity to read
how each feature is recorded.

03:14.933 --> 03:21.933
Find Phenotype search under Tables,
Phenotypes, at sysndd.dbmr.unibe.ch.

03:23.207 --> 03:26.461
The documentation explains each step.
